# TypeSafe Cheatsheet

## Setup
{: .col-2}

### Install

```elixir
# mix.exs
{:typesafe, "~> 0.1.0"}
```

```console
$ export TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...
```

### Build a client

```elixir
client = TypeSafe.new()
client = TypeSafe.new(api_key: key, model: "jev-preview")
client = TypeSafe.new(finch: [name: MyApp.Finch])
```

Options resolve in order: `new/1` option, `TYPESAFE_*` env var, `config :typesafe`, default.

## Questions
{: .col-2}

### Noul (yes/no)

```elixir
TypeSafe.noul("Does this convey urgency?")

TypeSafe.noul("Does this convey urgency?",
  criteria: %{true: "Explicitly time-sensitive", false: "No urgency expressed"}
)
```

### Choice (one of a set)

```elixir
# keyword list keeps option order
TypeSafe.choice("Which team should handle this?",
  billing: "Payments, invoicing, refunds",
  technical: "Bugs, outages, integrations",
  other: nil
)

TypeSafe.choice("Tone?", [:calm, :angry])
TypeSafe.choice("Tone?", %{calm: nil, angry: nil})
```

### Score (ordered levels)

```elixir
TypeSafe.score("How frustrated is the customer?",
  ["Calm", "Frustrated", "Very angry"]
)
```

At least two levels. Levels cannot be `nil`.

### Structured JSON and extra fields

```elixir
TypeSafe.choice(
  %{task: "Route the ticket", notes: ["Prefer billing for charges"]},
  [billing: %{covers: ["refunds", "charges"]}, other: nil],
  extra: %{"future_field" => true}
)
```

### Tuple-returning constructors

```elixir
{:ok, q} = TypeSafe.Question.Noul.new("Is this spam?")
{:ok, q} = TypeSafe.Question.Choice.new("Tone?", [:calm, :angry])
{:error, %TypeSafe.Error{type: :invalid_request}} =
  TypeSafe.Question.Score.new("Urgency?", ["Only one"])
```

## Asking
{: .col-2}

### ask/4

```elixir
{:ok, response} =
  TypeSafe.ask(client, "Help! My payouts are failing.", %{
    is_urgent: TypeSafe.noul("Does this convey urgency?")
  })
```

State can be a string, map or list. Questions can be a map or keyword list.

### ask!/4

```elixir
response = TypeSafe.ask!(client, state, questions)
# raises %TypeSafe.Error{} on failure
```

### Per-call options

```elixir
TypeSafe.ask(client, state, questions,
  model: "jev-preview",
  timeout: 20_000,
  retry: false,
  headers: [{"x-trace-id", trace_id}],
  telemetry_metadata: %{ticket_id: 42}
)
```

### list_models/2

```elixir
{:ok, [%TypeSafe.Model{name: "jev-latest"} | _]} =
  TypeSafe.list_models(client)
```

## Answers
{: .col-2}

### Noul

```elixir
answer.noul                                #=> 0.95
TypeSafe.Answer.Noul.yes?(answer)          #=> true (>= 0.5)
TypeSafe.Answer.Noul.yes?(answer, 0.97)    #=> false
```

### Choice

```elixir
answer.choice          #=> :billing
answer.probabilities   #=> %{billing: 0.87, technical: 0.13, sales: 0.0}
answer.confidence      #=> 0.81

TypeSafe.Answer.Choice.ranked(answer)
#=> [billing: 0.87, technical: 0.13, sales: 0.0]
TypeSafe.Answer.Choice.margin(answer)
#=> 0.74
```

### Score

```elixir
answer.score           #=> 1.05
answer.legend          #=> %{0 => "Calm", 1 => "Frustrated", 2 => "Very angry"}
answer.probabilities   #=> %{0 => 0.0, 1 => 0.95, 2 => 0.05}
answer.confidence      #=> 0.93

TypeSafe.Answer.Score.expected_level(answer)  #=> {1, "Frustrated"}
TypeSafe.Answer.Score.max_level(answer)       #=> {1, "Frustrated"}
TypeSafe.Answer.Score.ranked(answer)          #=> [{1, 0.95}, {2, 0.05}, {0, 0.0}]
```

### Response

```elixir
response.answers.is_urgent              # keyed by your ids
response.model                          #=> "jev-1.13.0"
response.usage                          #=> %TypeSafe.Usage{input_tokens: 414, output_tokens: 73}
response.request_id                     #=> "req_01a0..."
response.raw                            # decoded JSON body

TypeSafe.Response.fetch!(response, :is_urgent)
TypeSafe.Response.fetch(response, :missing)   #=> :error
TypeSafe.Response.nouls(response)             # also choices/1, scores/1
```

## Errors
{: .col-2}

### Matching

```elixir
case TypeSafe.ask(client, state, questions) do
  {:ok, response} -> response
  {:error, %TypeSafe.Error{type: :rate_limited, retry_after_ms: ms}} -> {:later, ms}
  {:error, %TypeSafe.Error{type: :invalid_request, path: path}} -> {:bug, path}
  {:error, %TypeSafe.Error{} = error} -> {:error, Exception.message(error)}
end

TypeSafe.Error.retryable?(error)
```

### Types

| `type` | Cause | Retried |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `:invalid_request` | failed validation before sending | no |
| `:bad_request` | HTTP 400 | no |
| `:authentication` | HTTP 401 | no |
| `:permission_denied` | HTTP 403 | no |
| `:not_found` | HTTP 404 | no |
| `:unprocessable` | HTTP 422 | no |
| `:rate_limited` | HTTP 429 | yes |
| `:overloaded` | HTTP 529 | yes |
| `:server` | other 5xx | yes |
| `:api` | other non-2xx | no |
| `:transport` | connection failure or pool timeout | yes |
| `:timeout` | request timed out | yes |
| `:invalid_response` | 2xx body failed decoding | no |

## Configuration
{: .col-2}

### Client options

| Option | Env var | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `:api_key` | `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` | required |
| `:base_url` | `TYPESAFE_BASE_URL` | `"https://api.typesafe.ai"` |
| `:model` | `TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL` | `"jev-latest"` |
| `:timeout` | | `10_000` ms (receive) |
| `:retry` | | `%TypeSafe.Retry{}` |
| `:headers` | | `[]` |
| `:finch` | | Req's default pool |
| `:req_options` | | `[]` (merged with config) |

### Retry policy

```elixir
TypeSafe.new(retry: false)
TypeSafe.new(retry: [max_retries: 4, budget_ms: 60_000])
```

| Option | Default |
| --- | --- |
| `:max_retries` | `2` |
| `:backoff_initial_ms` | `500` |
| `:backoff_max_ms` | `5_000` |
| `:jitter` | `0.25` |
| `:statuses` | `[408, 429, 500..599]` |
| `:respect_retry_after` | `true` |
| `:max_retry_after_ms` | `60_000` |
| `:retry_transport_errors` | `true` |
| `:budget_ms` | `30_000` |

### Application config

```elixir
# config/runtime.exs
config :typesafe,
  api_key: System.get_env("TYPESAFE_API_KEY"),
  model: "jev-latest"
```

### Telemetry events

| Event | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `[:typesafe, :request, :start]` | once per call |
| `[:typesafe, :request, :stop]` | `:duration`, tokens; `:result`, `:retries`, `:error` |
| `[:typesafe, :request, :exception]` | only on a raise |

## Testing
{: .col-2}

### config/test.exs

```elixir
config :typesafe,
  api_key: "test",
  retry: false,
  req_options: [plug: {Req.Test, TypeSafe}]
```

### Stub answers

```elixir
TypeSafe.Test.stub_answers(%{
  is_urgent: {:noul, 0.92},
  department: {:choice, :technical,
    %{billing: 0.08, technical: 0.85, sales: 0.07}, 0.82},
  frustration: {:score, 1.6, ["Calm", "Frustrated", "Very angry"],
    %{0 => 0.05, 1 => 0.3, 2 => 0.65}, 0.78}
})
```

### Stub failures

```elixir
TypeSafe.Test.stub_error(429, retry_after_ms: 1200)
TypeSafe.Test.stub_error(422, body: %{"detail" => "..."})
TypeSafe.Test.stub_transport_error(:timeout)
TypeSafe.Test.stub_models([%{name: "jev-latest"}])
```

### Sequences and other processes

```elixir
Req.Test.expect(TypeSafe, TypeSafe.Test.error_plug(529))
Req.Test.expect(TypeSafe, TypeSafe.Test.answers_plug(%{is_urgent: {:noul, 0.9}}))

Req.Test.allow(TypeSafe, self(), pid)
```

## Tools
{: .col-2}

### JSON Schemas

```console
$ mix typesafe.schema
$ mix typesafe.schema --output schemas/typesafe
$ mix typesafe.schema --check
```

### Existing Req pipelines

```elixir
req = TypeSafe.Req.attach(Req.new(), api_key: key)

req
|> Req.post(typesafe_state: text, typesafe_questions: questions)
|> TypeSafe.Req.decode(questions)
```
